---
// The shapes bh plan knows how to file, nested the way their dotted ids
// nest, and what each tier maps to in git and in the org chart.
// Source: docs/PLANNING-PLANE.md (spec, two gates, fidelity tiers),
// docs/AGF.md (workstream = epic of epics; the dotted id is the tier),
// bh plugin dispatcher/references/workstream-tier.md (nesting cap → a deeper
// tier runs as its own supervised session). "Roadmap" is the name this site
// gives that outermost tier; it is a direction label, not a verb.
const hex = (cx: number, cy: number, r = 11) =>
  `${cx - r},${cy} ${cx - r / 2},${cy - r * 0.866} ${cx + r / 2},${cy - r * 0.866} ${cx + r},${cy} ${cx + r / 2},${cy + r * 0.866} ${cx - r / 2},${cy + r * 0.866}`;
---
<figure id="fig-plan-shapes">
  <div class="diagram">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1160 560" role="img"
      aria-label="Nested shapes diagram. Inside a dashed roadmap boundary sit two workstreams; inside a workstream sit two epics, each a molecule of dependency-linked issues with a kickoff gate on every root issue; a spike molecule variant shows spike beads feeding a decision bead. To the right, a table maps each tier to its id shape, branch namespace and seat, and a panel lists what bh plan file compiles: the epic record, children with required acceptance and the identity triplet plus dimension labels, the dependency DAG, the bd swarm, and one kickoff gate per root, resolved by bh plan approve. Fidelity tiers quick, spec and deep scale the research, not the shape.">
      <defs>
        <marker id="ps-n" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="var(--ink-3)"/></marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- ===== nested shapes ===== -->
      <text class="d-kicker" x="24" y="28">THE SHAPES — THE DOTTED ID IS THE TIER</text>

      <!-- roadmap (direction) -->
      <rect class="d-box-dir" x="24" y="40" width="640" height="478" rx="10"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="40" y="62">roadmap</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="108" y="62">an ordered set of workstreams · above the Task-nesting cap, so it runs as its own session</text>
      <rect class="d-chip-dir" x="570" y="48" width="80" height="14" rx="7"/>
      <text class="d-mute" x="610" y="59" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:9.5px">direction · naming</text>

      <!-- workstream -->
      <rect class="d-box" x="40" y="76" width="608" height="300" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="54" y="98">workstream · bh-ws</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="200" y="98">issue_type=epic whose children are epics — no new type, no new rule</text>

      <!-- epic 1 -->
      <rect class="d-box-h" x="54" y="112" width="282" height="150" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="68" y="132">epic · bh-ws.1</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="170" y="132">issues + dependency DAG</text>
      <!-- issues a -> b -> c, a is root -->
      <polygon class="gatehex" points={hex(96, 186)}/>
      <rect class="node" x="112" y="172" width="54" height="28"/>
      <text class="nlabel" x="139" y="190" style="font-size:11px">.1.1</text>
      <path class="flow" d="M 166 186 H 194" marker-end="url(#ps-n)"/>
      <rect class="node" x="198" y="172" width="54" height="28"/>
      <text class="nlabel" x="225" y="190" style="font-size:11px">.1.2</text>
      <path class="flow" d="M 252 186 H 280" marker-end="url(#ps-n)"/>
      <rect class="node" x="284" y="172" width="42" height="28"/>
      <text class="nlabel" x="305" y="190" style="font-size:11px">.1.3</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="68" y="226">a linear chain with no mid-point testable unit:</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="68" y="240">a batch:&lt;group&gt; candidate (≤ 5, cohesive, one model tier)</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="68" y="254">leaf → wt/bead/issue/bh-ws.1.2 · developer</text>

      <!-- epic 2 -->
      <rect class="d-box-h" x="352" y="112" width="282" height="150" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="366" y="132">epic · bh-ws.2</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="468" y="132">two roots, one join</text>
      <polygon class="gatehex" points={hex(394, 166)}/>
      <rect class="node" x="410" y="152" width="54" height="28"/>
      <text class="nlabel" x="437" y="170" style="font-size:11px">.2.1</text>
      <polygon class="gatehex" points={hex(394, 212)}/>
      <rect class="node" x="410" y="198" width="54" height="28"/>
      <text class="nlabel" x="437" y="216" style="font-size:11px">.2.2</text>
      <path class="flow" d="M 464 166 C 500 166, 500 186, 530 188" marker-end="url(#ps-n)"/>
      <path class="flow" d="M 464 212 C 500 212, 500 192, 530 190" marker-end="url(#ps-n)"/>
      <rect class="node" x="534" y="175" width="54" height="28"/>
      <text class="nlabel" x="561" y="193" style="font-size:11px">.2.3</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="366" y="240">every root carries its own kickoff gate;</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="366" y="254">bh plan approve resolves them all, idempotently</text>

      <!-- spike variant -->
      <rect class="d-box" x="54" y="276" width="580" height="88" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-title" x="68" y="296">spike molecule · bh-ws.3</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="262" y="296">same shape, two labels: epic tag:spike + one tag:decision bead depending on every spike</text>
      <polygon class="gatehex" points={hex(96, 334)}/>
      <rect class="node" x="112" y="320" width="80" height="28"/>
      <text class="nlabel" x="152" y="338" style="font-size:11px">spike .3.1</text>
      <polygon class="gatehex" points={hex(232, 334)}/>
      <rect class="node" x="248" y="320" width="80" height="28"/>
      <text class="nlabel" x="288" y="338" style="font-size:11px">spike .3.2</text>
      <path class="flow" d="M 192 326 C 230 302, 330 302, 380 328" marker-end="url(#ps-n)"/>
      <path class="flow" d="M 328 334 H 380" marker-end="url(#ps-n)"/>
      <rect class="node" x="384" y="320" width="94" height="28"/>
      <text class="nlabel" x="431" y="338" style="font-size:11px">decision .3.3</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="492" y="330">acceptance = a verdict doc,</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="492" y="344">never product code</text>

      <!-- second workstream placeholder -->
      <rect class="d-chip-dir" x="40" y="392" width="608" height="36" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-mute" x="54" y="414">workstream · bh-ws2 — same machinery; a roadmap orders workstreams by their dependency edges, nothing more</text>

      <!-- tier table -->
      <line class="d-sep" x1="40" y1="444" x2="648" y2="444"/>
      <text class="d-code-h" x="40" y="464">tier</text><text class="d-code-h" x="150" y="464">id shape</text><text class="d-code-h" x="290" y="464">branch</text><text class="d-code-h" x="470" y="464">seat</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="40" y="482">issue</text><text class="d-code" x="150" y="482">bh-ws.2.1</text><text class="d-code" x="290" y="482">wt/bead/issue/&lt;id&gt;</text><text class="d-mute" x="470" y="482">developer · dev/</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="40" y="496">epic (molecule)</text><text class="d-code" x="150" y="496">bh-ws.2</text><text class="d-code" x="290" y="496">wt/bead/epic/&lt;id&gt;</text><text class="d-mute" x="470" y="496">dispatcher · disp/ — nested under a workstream</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="40" y="510">workstream</text><text class="d-code" x="150" y="510">bh-ws</text><text class="d-code" x="290" y="510">wt/bead/epic/&lt;id&gt;</text><text class="d-mute" x="470" y="510">dispatcher · disp/ (root of its session)</text>

      <!-- ===== what plan file compiles ===== -->
      <text class="d-kicker" x="690" y="28">WHAT bh plan file COMPILES</text>
      {[
        { y: 44,  t: 'epic record',          s: 'title · description · design · complexity (explicit or inferred) · adopts / external_ref provenance' },
        { y: 92,  t: 'children, in topo order', s: 'acceptance REQUIRED · identity triplet · closed dims: size, complexity, harness, component' },
        { y: 140, t: 'open dims',             s: 'batch:<group> · tag: · wave: · model: <provider>/<name> — labels, so membership survives filing' },
        { y: 188, t: 'dependency DAG',        s: 'deps: closed set, acyclic, no orphans · bd swarm create wires it · bh plan show round-trips it' },
        { y: 236, t: 'one kickoff gate per root', s: 'a type:human bd gate blocking each root · kickoff=pending on the epic' },
      ].map((r) => (
        <g>
          <rect class="d-chip" x="690" y={r.y} width="446" height="40" rx="6"/>
          <text class="d-title" x="704" y={r.y + 17} style="font-size:12px">{r.t}</text>
          <text class="d-mute" x="704" y={r.y + 32} style="font-size:9.5px">{r.s}</text>
        </g>
      ))}

      <!-- two gates -->
      <polygon class="gatehex" points={`${hex(716, 316, 22)}`}/>
      <text class="glabel" x="716" y="314" style="font-size:9px">PLAN</text>
      <text class="glabel" x="716" y="324" style="font-size:8px">approval</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="748" y="312">bh plan file &lt;spec&gt;</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="748" y="326">is the decomposition right?</text>
      <path class="flow" d="M 900 316 H 930" marker-end="url(#ps-n)"/>
      <polygon class="gatehex" points={`${hex(960, 316, 22)}`}/>
      <text class="glabel" x="960" y="314" style="font-size:9px">KICKOFF</text>
      <text class="glabel" x="960" y="324" style="font-size:8px">approval</text>
      <text class="d-code" x="992" y="312">bh plan approve &lt;epic&gt;</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="992" y="326">should it start now?</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="690" y="352">never collapsed into one. Then roots surface in bd ready and dispatch may start.</text>

      <!-- fidelity -->
      <line class="d-sep" x1="690" y1="368" x2="1136" y2="368"/>
      <text class="d-kicker" x="690" y="390">FIDELITY — SCALES THE RESEARCH, NOT THE SHAPE</text>
      <text class="d-code-h" x="690" y="412">quick</text><text class="d-mute" x="760" y="412">≈ 2–4 issues · inline spec · dry-run · file</text>
      <text class="d-code-h" x="690" y="430">spec</text><text class="d-mute" x="760" y="430">≈ 5–15 issues · YAML spec authored, checked, previewed</text>
      <text class="d-code-h" x="690" y="448">deep</text><text class="d-mute" x="760" y="448">cross-cutting · analyst sub-agents research first</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="690" y="472">All three converge on the same compiler and the same two gates. After filing,</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="690" y="486">beads is the source of truth; the spec is absorbed scaffolding.</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="690" y="508">Re-entry: replan is scoped to ONE molecule and ONE triggering event (a spike</text>
      <text class="d-mute" x="690" y="522">verdict, a mid-execution blocker); groom is backlog-wide hygiene with no trigger.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <div class="legend display">
    <span><span class="sw hex"></span>kickoff gate on a root bead</span>
    <span><span class="sw" style="background:var(--honey)"></span>molecule (epic)</span>
    <span><span class="sw dash"></span>direction / naming</span>
  </div>
  <figcaption>There is one shape, applied recursively. A <b>molecule</b> is an epic with
  dependency-linked issues; a <b>workstream</b> is an epic whose children are epics; the position in
  the dotted id is the tier, and every container tier gets the same branch namespace, the same
  dispatcher seat and the same <code>finish</code> rule. A <b>spike molecule</b> is that shape with
  two labels. What this site calls a <b>roadmap</b> is the tier above a workstream — an ordered set
  of workstreams — and because live sub-agent nesting is capped at two levels, it runs as its own
  supervised session rather than as a nested Task; the name is a convention here, not a verb.
  The compiler is where accuracy is enforced: acceptance is required on every child, dependencies
  must form a closed acyclic set, and a hand-assembled epic that lacks any of this plumbing is
  refused by <code>approve</code> and <code>start</code> until <code>bh plan repair</code> converges
  it.</figcaption>
</figure>
